From: NanoKVM build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: cv1800b_sdhci: honor 'no-1-8-v' DT property

Backport of the upstream fix (merged after v2026.01). Without it, the SD
card fails to initialize under U-Boot on 3.3V-only boards (LicheeRV Nano):
sdhci_setup_cfg() re-adds UHS caps from the controller, U-Boot issues a
1.8V switch the board can't do, and the card stops responding
("Card did not respond to voltage select! : -110"). Setting
SDHCI_QUIRK_NO_1_8_V masks the UHS caps so init proceeds at 3.3V.
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/cv1800b_sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/cv1800b_sdhci.c
index 036e798..0610185 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/cv1800b_sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/cv1800b_sdhci.c
@@ -98,6 +98,17 @@ static int cv1800b_sdhci_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * sdhci_setup_cfg() re-adds the UHS (SDR104/SDR50/DDR50) caps from the
+	 * controller's CAPABILITIES_1 even when the DT says no-1-8-v; U-Boot then
+	 * issues CMD11 to switch to 1.8V, the card switches but the bus stays at
+	 * 3.3V, and the card wedges ("Card did not respond to voltage select!").
+	 * Mask the UHS caps out. Backport of upstream commit "mmc: cv1800b_sdhci:
+	 * honor 'no-1-8-v' DT property" (merged after v2026.01).
+	 */
+	if (dev_read_bool(dev, "no-1-8-v"))
+		host->quirks |= SDHCI_QUIRK_NO_1_8_V;
+
 	ret = sdhci_setup_cfg(&plat->cfg, host, 0, 200000);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
